xpilot-ref patch 0006: optional default-robot decision trace in the server.

This patch modifies XPilot 4.5.5 (GPL-2.0-or-later, Copyright (C) 1991-2010
by Bjoern Stabell, Ken Ronny Schouten, Bert Gijsbers, Dick Balaska et al.).
It is a derivative work distributed under the same license.

Why: to compare a reimplementation's default robot (robotdef.c) decisions
against the original server, e.g. the robot mode while a robot is stuck at
a wall.  Inert unless the environment variable XPILOT_TRACE_ROBOT is set;
then every Robot_default_play() call is followed by one line "XPROBOT loop
frame id mode longterm lock evaded turnacc power thrusting x y name" on
stderr (evaded = 1 when the play returned through Check_robot_evade()).
Game logic and the random sequence are unchanged.

--- a/src/server/robotdef.c
+++ b/src/server/robotdef.c
@@ -96,6 +96,7 @@
 static void Robot_default_create(int ind, char *str);
 static void Robot_default_go_home(int ind);
 static void Robot_default_play(int ind);
+static void Robot_default_play_trace(int ind);
 static void Robot_default_set_war(int ind, int victim_id);
 static int Robot_default_war_on_player(int ind);
 static void Robot_default_message(int ind, const char *str);
@@ -109,6 +110,7 @@
  */
 static DFLOAT	Visibility_distance;
 static DFLOAT	Max_enemy_distance;
+static int	xpref_evaded;	/* xpilot-ref robot trace */
 
 
 /*
@@ -119,7 +121,7 @@
     Robot_default_round_tick,
